    "hypotheses": [
      "Evidence responsiveness is strong on selected failures; it does not show that CPT encoded or failed to encode the facts.",
      "CPT+SFT reference-answer NLL is lower than SFT-only while greedy short-answer full credit is lower. Better reference likelihood does not guarantee the most probable generated answer is correct.",
      "Thinking helps the base on this subset but not SFT models; turning thinking off is not a universal improvement.",
      "The 128-token cap truncates 18/23 base and CPT responses. Raising it to 768 eliminates those truncations without increasing aggregate full credit.",
      "Apparent cloze base-to-CPT gain includes two formatting-only deductions. Do not attribute the full 1/8 to 4/8 shift to new knowledge.",
      "The APC cloze omits tumor-suppressor disambiguation and the TLR4 cloze has an unresolved this-gene antecedent. These probes confound knowledge with missing context.",
